{
  "title": "Three Files One Relation Each",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Three places record overlapping facts about the same set of practices. The split that keeps them from drifting.",
      "id": "2fc5a0f67a5594aa"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "fc4bc56fb9ed2926",
      "text": "<svg style=\"width:100%;height:auto;display:block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1053 818\"><rect width=\"1053\" height=\"818\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n      <defs id=\"svg-defs\"><marker id=\"mk000000\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkc53030\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#c53030\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkc05621\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#c05621\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkb7791f\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#b7791f\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk276749\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#276749\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk2b4c7e\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#2b4c7e\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk553c9a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#553c9a\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk97266d\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#97266d\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk234e52\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#234e52\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk1a202c\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#1a202c\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk3b82f6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkf59e0b\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk8b5cf6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk7c3aed\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk0E5A4B\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#0E5A4B\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk8A5F10\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#8A5F10\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk2C5F8A\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#2C5F8A\"/></marker></defs>\n      \n      <g id=\"wardley-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"lop-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"lines-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"edges-layer\"><g id=\"edge-f1\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 A method names the skills it requires; the registry certifies them. This is the join between the pathway layer and the person layer.</title><path d=\"M588.2799157477289,69.64316292900068 Q440,4.400000000000006 291.7200842522712,69.64316292900068\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" marker-end=\"url(#mk0E5A4B)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"440\" cy=\"7.021581464500343\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"REQUIRES_SKILL\" href=\"/requiresskill.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"440\" y=\"19.021581464500343\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#0E5A4B\">REQUIRES_SKILL</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-f2\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Each step names one tool. The tool is the instrument, not the point — the step's question is the point.</title><path d=\"M771.7200842522711,150.35683707099932 Q920,215.6 1068.2799157477289,150.35683707099932\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" marker-end=\"url(#mk0E5A4B)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"920\" cy=\"212.97841853549966\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"USES\" href=\"/uses.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"920\" y=\"200.97841853549966\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#0E5A4B\">USES</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-f3\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 A tool that IS a method wearing a tool's clothes — A3 Problem Solving, the eVSM cycle. Build it as a tool, give it a method page, and have the two point at each other.</title><path d=\"M1068.2799157477289,69.64316292900068 Q920,4.400000000000006 771.7200842522711,69.64316292900068\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"2.6\" marker-end=\"url(#mk0E5A4B)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"920\" cy=\"7.021581464500343\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"EMBODIES\" href=\"/embodies.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"920\" y=\"19.021581464500343\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#0E5A4B\">EMBODIES</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-d1\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 A Do One earns the first star. A Teach One whose learner then runs it earns the second — the method crossed a person boundary, which is the real test.</title><path d=\"M215.90633347652505,164.61689261680607 Q261.8,322.2 372.8568507157464,377\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk8A5F10)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"262.0274094086928\" cy=\"321.8413028926786\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Do One / Teach One\" href=\"/do-one--teach-one.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(53.5,268.5,311.7)\"><tspan x=\"268.4527640644428\" y=\"311.70647099728774\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#8A5F10\">Do One / Teach One</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-d2\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Active means at least one credential issued and the teaching chain begun. Ready means a mentor exists. Candidate means nominated, no mentor yet.</title><path d=\"M247.01812964316616,161.55643030425244 Q481.8,419 775,419.701099952176\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk8A5F10)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"489.7485791345656\" cy=\"384.06670359996167\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"mentor + chain\" href=\"/mentor--chain.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(26.1,492.4,372.4)\"><tspan x=\"492.410960445056\" y=\"372.36577518561984\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#8A5F10\">mentor + chain</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-d3\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Written onto the method as a computed field, never authored. If attestation is high-friction nobody logs runs, and untested becomes indistinguishable from unlogged — that is the risk that would kill the whole signal.</title><path d=\"M531.8818011257035,377 Q638.2,313.4 668.7365570376721,164.80823680711705\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk8A5F10)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"639.2198326128172\" cy=\"314.54377796289765\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"marks\" href=\"/marks.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(-57.2,631.2,305.6)\"><tspan x=\"631.2337353840279\" y=\"305.5870904584503\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#8A5F10\">marks</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-d4\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Also computed. Together the two axes expose different failures, which is why collapsing them would hide exactly what each is built to reveal.</title><path d=\"M891.1632251720747,377 Q858.2,216.6 755.9919980019083,155.45873730080484\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\" marker-end=\"url(#mk8A5F10)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"858.053335825786\" cy=\"216.81023536224728\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"marks\" href=\"/marks.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(58.6,851.2,226.7)\"><tspan x=\"851.1875238128699\" y=\"226.65201494742885\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#8A5F10\">marks</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-p1\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Skills and attestations become nodes and edges. The confidence query counts attestations by type and by NDC.</title><path d=\"M217.05869067202585,164.55914008212636 Q319,490.6 606.3498119592591,625.4394962490263\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2C5F8A\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\" marker-end=\"url(#mk2C5F8A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"344.4676855754029\" cy=\"464.3366078556269\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-p2\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Pathways become ordered step chains. HANDS_OFF_TO edges are what a shortest-path query traverses.</title><path d=\"M656.1796933253338,164.13706062424146 Q559,385 660.4871065087182,615.6525147925413\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2C5F8A\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\" marker-end=\"url(#mk2C5F8A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"578.7030561478498\" cy=\"385.97089475574984\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-p3\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Tools become nodes. 'What methods use this tool' stops being a script and becomes one hop.</title><path d=\"M1071.4948073300047,151.53124553544927 Q799,279.4 693.9657529275211,615.3330624855923\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2C5F8A\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\" marker-end=\"url(#mk2C5F8A)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"822.0552555856779\" cy=\"308.04540637094124\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g></g>\n      <g id=\"nodes-layer\"><g id=\"node-reg\" transform=\"translate(200,110)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 v0.1 · 31 skills · 1 live credential. What a person can be certified in.  —  Already exists, dated 1 March 2026, on Models for Seeing Systems. Causal Loop Diagramming is Active — first mentor Kerry Turner, first credential Marc Pierson, 10 December 2025. The most developed of the three files, so it seeds the others rather than being replaced.</title><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"-46\" rx=\"135\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"-135\" y=\"-46\" width=\"270\" height=\"101\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"-135\" y1=\"-46\" x2=\"-135\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"135\" y1=\"-46\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"135\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"131\" cy=\"-51\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"SODOTO Registry SKILLS\" href=\"/sodoto-registry-skills.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#0B3B31\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">SODOTO Registry SKILLS</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-meth\" transform=\"translate(680,110)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Ordered uses of tools. Each step carries question, gate and handoff; each method carries a fallback.  —  Sequence lives here and nowhere else, because a hammer is used in many processes and does a different job in each. Steps carry the question they answer, any gate that must hold first, and the handoff to the next step.</title><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"-46\" rx=\"135\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"-135\" y=\"-46\" width=\"270\" height=\"101\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"-135\" y1=\"-46\" x2=\"-135\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"135\" y1=\"-46\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"135\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"131\" cy=\"-51\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"methods.json PATHWAYS\" href=\"/methodsjson-pathways.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#0B3B31\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">methods.json PATHWAYS</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-cat\" transform=\"translate(1160,110)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 id · what · shelf · status · launch · intro · manual · example · deck. What you can open.  —  No methods field. A tool cannot carry sequence. Shelving is a property here, not a folder on disk, because one tool sits on several shelves — the Graph Tool answers Why, How-strategy and How-mechanism.</title><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"-46\" rx=\"135\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"-135\" y=\"-46\" width=\"270\" height=\"101\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"-135\" y1=\"-46\" x2=\"-135\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"135\" y1=\"-46\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"135\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#0E5A4B\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"131\" cy=\"-51\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"catalog.json TOOLS\" href=\"/catalogjson-tools.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#0B3B31\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">catalog.json TOOLS</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-conf\" transform=\"translate(460,420)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Values: two stars, one star, none, retired.  —  Derived from Do One and Teach One attestations on the method itself. Because a star is computed from signed credentials it cannot be talked up. Zero stars is a normal, publishable state.</title><rect x=\"-115\" y=\"-43\" width=\"230\" height=\"86\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#F3EBDA\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"-39\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"CONFIDENCE\" href=\"/confidence.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#513809\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">CONFIDENCE</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-trans\" transform=\"translate(900,420)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Values: Active, Ready, Candidate.  —  Marc's own axis, five months older than the star scheme. Read off whether the method's constituent skills have mentors and teaching chains. Orthogonal to confidence: a method can be proven and untransmissible, or teachable and untested.</title><rect x=\"-125\" y=\"-43\" width=\"250\" height=\"86\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#F3EBDA\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><circle cx=\"121\" cy=\"-39\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"TRANSMISSIBILITY\" href=\"/transmissibility.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#513809\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">TRANSMISSIBILITY</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-neo\" transform=\"translate(680,660)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Queries it makes cheap: derived back-links, impact analysis before a rename, gap-finding, path-finding, confidence, staleness.  —  If the database is down the storefront still works and the handout still opens. Nothing load-bearing sits only in the graph. Same arrangement as the SODOTO projector.</title><rect x=\"-115\" y=\"-45\" width=\"230\" height=\"90\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#EEF1F5\" stroke=\"#2C5F8A\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><line x1=\"-97\" y1=\"-45\" x2=\"-97\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#2C5F8A\" stroke-width=\"1\" opacity=\".35\"/><line x1=\"97\" y1=\"-45\" x2=\"97\" y2=\"45\" stroke=\"#2C5F8A\" stroke-width=\"1\" opacity=\".35\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"-41\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Neo4j\" href=\"/neo4j.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1B3B57\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">Neo4j</tspan></text></a></g></g>\n      <g id=\"triples-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"drag-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"eip-statement-layer\"/>\n      \n      <g id=\"opm-symbols-chart\"/>\n    </svg>"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "- The [[SODOTO]] Skills Registry holds skills — what a person can be certified in. Version 0.1, 31 skills, one live credential.\n- methods.json holds pathways — ordered uses of tools. Each step carries the question it answers, any gate that must hold first, and the handoff to the next step.\n- catalog.json holds tools — what you can launch. It has no methods field, because a tool cannot carry sequence.",
      "id": "5d40fbf15bfecee8"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "One relation each: a method requires a skill, a method uses a tool, and a tool may embody a method.",
      "id": "6483b59192743323"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Two status axes, not one",
      "id": "6bc7bec6d950f23a"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Confidence answers \"does this method hold?\" and is derived from Do One and Teach One attestations on the method itself. A Do One earns the first star; a Teach One whose learner then runs it earns the second. Because a star is computed from signed credentials it cannot be talked up. Zero stars is a normal, publishable state.",
      "id": "6c58dec82ac10d10"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Transmissibility answers \"can this method be taught?\" and is read off the registry's Active, Ready and Candidate. It measures whether the method's constituent skills have mentors and teaching chains.",
      "id": "c2bbfb7866765c61"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "These are orthogonal and both are needed. A method can be well-proven and untransmissible — it works, but only its author can run it. Or highly transmissible and untested — everyone could learn it, nobody has tried it. Collapsing them would hide exactly the failure each is built to expose.",
      "id": "434e357f66ac8525"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Neo4j is a projection",
      "id": "24d804b3546054f5"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "The three files stay the human-editable, git-diffable source. Neo4j is rebuilt from them. If the database is down the storefront still works and the handout still opens; nothing load-bearing sits only in the graph.",
      "id": "c24eb743f19c0a93"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "What it makes cheap: derived back-links, impact analysis before a rename, gap-finding, path-finding from what you have to what you need, the confidence computation, and staleness.",
      "id": "77f1be76211cd9ce"
    }
  ],
