      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "6c58dec82ac10d10",
        "text": "Confidence answers \"does this method hold?\" and is derived from Do One and Teach One attestations on the method itself. A Do One earns the first star; a Teach One whose learner then runs it earns the second. Because a star is computed from signed credentials it cannot be talked up. Zero stars is a normal, publishable state."
      },
      "date": 1787091019591,
      "after": "6bc7bec6d950f23a"
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "c2bbfb7866765c61",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "c2bbfb7866765c61",
        "text": "Transmissibility answers \"can this method be taught?\" and is read off the registry's Active, Ready and Candidate. It measures whether the method's constituent skills have mentors and teaching chains."
      },
      "date": 1787091019592,
      "after": "6c58dec82ac10d10"
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "434e357f66ac8525",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "434e357f66ac8525",
        "text": "These are orthogonal and both are needed. A method can be well-proven and untransmissible — it works, but only its author can run it. Or highly transmissible and untested — everyone could learn it, nobody has tried it. Collapsing them would hide exactly the failure each is built to expose."
      },
      "date": 1787091019593,
      "after": "c2bbfb7866765c61"
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "24d804b3546054f5",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "24d804b3546054f5",
        "text": "## Neo4j is a projection"
      },
      "date": 1787091019594,
      "after": "434e357f66ac8525"
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "c24eb743f19c0a93",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "c24eb743f19c0a93",
        "text": "The three files stay the human-editable, git-diffable source. Neo4j is rebuilt from them. If the database is down the storefront still works and the handout still opens; nothing load-bearing sits only in the graph."
      },
      "date": 1787091019595,
      "after": "24d804b3546054f5"
    },
    {
      "type": "add",
      "id": "77f1be76211cd9ce",
      "item": {
        "type": "markdown",
        "id": "77f1be76211cd9ce",
        "text": "What it makes cheap: derived back-links, impact analysis before a rename, gap-finding, path-finding from what you have to what you need, the confidence computation, and staleness."
      },
      "date": 1787091019596,
      "after": "c24eb743f19c0a93"
    }
  ]
}